{"title":"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Bijection)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Bijection)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(🚀Just_2_min🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (🚀Just 2 min🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical(Comprehensive🧠🧠)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical(Comprehensive🧠🧠)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many three-digit positive integers have an odd number of even digits?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/482b4f850c6e1ea042cee85e0906376ad761dead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }150\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }250\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }350\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }450\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }550$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"446\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use simple case work to solve this problem.\n</p><p>Case 1: even, even, even = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9e3da4ed129c95513a9b561d04d21fcd415568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Case 2: even, odd, odd = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9e3da4ed129c95513a9b561d04d21fcd415568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Case 3: odd, even, odd = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410e601fb97e2839e8a6b51e27ffcf212ffde45c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Case 4: odd, odd, even = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410e601fb97e2839e8a6b51e27ffcf212ffde45c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Simply sum up the cases to get your answer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c2ab5f486051695f32773f4d0a9e8914a1b8272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 + 100 + 125 + 125 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)~}450}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"276\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>- Wesseywes7254\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Bijection.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Bijection)\">Solution 2 (Bijection)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Bijection)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will show that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/4739126bff84658daf38a400b94af84c72f11fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$450$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> by proving a bijection between the three digit integers that have an even number of even digits and the three digit integers that have an odd number of even digits. For every even number with an odd number of even digits, we increment the number's last digit by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, unless the last digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, in which case it becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. It is very easy to show that every number with an even number of even digits is mapped to every number with an odd number of even digits, and vice versa. Thus, the answer is half the number of three digit numbers, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/7286c460461eee8ab7c3f93a5d9ba6ca0a534276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)~}450}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy100\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are 9 possibilities for the first choice of a three-digit number in the hundreds place, excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now we have a few cases:\n</p><p>Case 1: The first digit is odd\n</p><p>In this case, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even digit is permitted, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is impossible. The even digit can be either in the tens or the ones, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a516ff027e840b5620c442f83a9607f630063ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot5\\cdot2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> ways to place the even digit and odd digit.\n</p><p>Case 2: The first digit is even\n</p><p>In this case, either all digits can be even or the rest of the digits can be odd. That's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced391def176c2a2955337ded30d70feec2bb1a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot5$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> for both of them, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a516ff027e840b5620c442f83a9607f630063ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot5\\cdot2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> in total.\n</p><p>Thus, both cases result in multiplying the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a516ff027e840b5620c442f83a9607f630063ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot5\\cdot2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/7286c460461eee8ab7c3f93a5d9ba6ca0a534276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)~}450}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-ichang3765\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28.F0.9F.9A.80Just_2_min.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(🚀Just_2_min🚀)\">Video Solution 1 (🚀Just 2 min🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (🚀Just 2 min🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rAad-1GMgIs\">https://youtu.be/rAad-1GMgIs</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_KNR0JV5rdI?t=167\">https://youtu.be/_KNR0JV5rdI?t=167</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical.28Comprehensive.F0.9F.A7.A0.F0.9F.A7.A0.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical(Comprehensive🧠🧠)\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical(Comprehensive🧠🧠)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Ani_lytical(Comprehensive🧠🧠)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/x3dmqfXpo7w?si=m-qcHA9WlxApnTtu\">https://youtu.be/x3dmqfXpo7w?si=m-qcHA9WlxApnTtu</a>\n</p><p>~Ani_lytical\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B\">2022 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Prob